CLI. At deploy time, if the directory is inside a git repo, capture: remote URL (origin, normalized to https://github.com/org/repo), branch, short and full commit SHA, and whether the working tree is dirty. Send them with the deploy. Print ✓ source: github.com/acme/tools @ main a3f8e21 and, if dirty, ⚠ uncommitted changes deployed — commit before sharing. If not a git repo, send nothing and print source: not a git repo.

Control plane. Store repo_url, branch, commit, dirty, deployed_at on a deploys table — one row per deploy, so history is kept — and the latest on the app row. Add GET /api/apps/<slug>/deploys.

Repo visibility. Don't assume. On deploy, the control plane hits https://api.github.com/repos/<org>/<repo> unauthenticated; 200 means public, 404 means private or nonexistent. Store repo_public. Never store a token.

Web UI. On /apps/<slug>, under the title: main · a3f8e21 · deployed 2 hours ago. If the repo is public, the commit is a link to https://github.com/org/repo/tree/<sha> — the commit tree, not the branch — and the runbook's Files table links each file to it at that SHA. If private, show the SHA as text and a quiet private repo label. A Deploys tab lists history: when, who, commit, dirty flag.

Runbook. Add a line at the top: Deployed from github.com/acme/tools @ a3f8e21 (main). If dirty: Deployed with uncommitted changes.

Drift. In the UI, if the branch's current HEAD on GitHub (public repos only, cached hourly) differs from the deployed commit, show 3 commits behind main next to the SHA. That's the whole point of recording it.

Test. Deploy examples/counter from a repo at a known commit; assert the app row has the SHA and the UI links to the tree URL. Make a commit without deploying; assert the drift label appears.

