593: };"}},"label":"answer-1","response":{"answer":"The request's stated purpose was provenance for accountability: the control plane records exactly what was deployed (repo, branch, commit SHA, dirty flag) so 'the UI can link to it and nobody confuses what's deployed with what's on main' — i.e. main can move ahead of what's actually running, so showing 'main' alone wouldn't tell you the real deployed state. The dirty flag exists to flag when the deployed code doesn't even match a commit at all (uncommitted local changes), which the CLI surfaces with a warning at deploy time: '⚠ uncommitted changes deployed — commit before sharing' (m4770). This is also why the SHA is stored per-deploy in a `deploys` table (history) and mirrored on the app row as the 'latest' — and why a non-git deploy explicitly clears the app-row copy rather than leaving stale repo info, since 'stale repo info under a fresh deployed_at would claim the deployed code matches a commit it doesn't' (packages/control-plane/src/index.js:138-140). The originally-planned drift feature ('3 commits behind main') was meant to use this same SHA to detect exactly this main-vs-deployed gap, but that UI/drift piece was explicitly deferred, not shipped, per the assistant's scope note (m4869) and the spec's deferred section (docs/features/source-provenance.md:23-26).

Next step: if you want the main-vs-deployed comparison surfaced, the deferred drift feature (GitHub compare, cached hourly, public repos only) is the recorded design to pick up.","citations":[{"kind":"message","message_id":"m4770"},{"kind":"message","message_id":"m4869"},{"end_line":150,"kind":"code","path":"packages/control-plane/src/index.js","start_line":138},{"end_line":26,"kind":"code","path":"docs/features/source-provenance.md","start_line":23}]}},{"available_context":{"decisions":[{"alternatives":["Store a GitHub token for authenticated/private-repo checks or linking"],"anchors":[{"end_line":97,"path":"packages/control-plane/src/index.js","start_line":85}],"constraints":["Unauthenticated GitHub API rate limit (60 req/h) shared across egress IPs"],"decision":"Determine repo visibility via an unauthenticated GET to the GitHub API (200=public, 404=private/nonexistent, other=unknown) and never store a token","depends_on":[],"evidence":[{"message_id":"m4770","quote":"On deploy, the control plane hits https://api.github.com/repos/<org>/<repo> unauthenticated; 200 means public, 404 means private or nonexistent. Store repo_public. Never store a token."}],"id":"d2","kind":"design","reason":"Explicit requirement: 'Don't assume... unauthenticated; 200 means public, 404 means private or nonexistent... Never store a token.'","revisit":null},{"alternatives":["Leave previous repo_url/branch/commit values in place when source is absent"],"anchors":[{"end_line":150,"path":"packages/control-plane/src/index.js","start_line":138}],"constraints":[],"decision":"When a deploy has no git source, clear the app-row provenance mirror columns rather than leaving stale values","depends_on":[],"evidence":[{"message_id":"m5108","quote":"`apiDeploy` stores both; no source clears the app-row copy (stale repo info must not outlive a non-git deploy)."}],"id":"d3","kind":"design","reason":"stale repo info must not outlive a non-git deploy","revisit":null},{"alternatives":["Keep the ALTER and handle the resulting failure some other way"],"anchors":[{"end_line":18,"path":"packages/control-plane/migrations/0003-provenance.sql","start_line":17}],"constraints":["Production DB previously had orphan deployed_at and dead runbook columns added manually"],"decision":"Drop the deployed_at ALTER from migration 0003-provenance.sql because the production apps table already has that column from an earlier manual experiment","depends_on":[],"evidence":[{"message_id":"m5142","quote":"Fix: drop the `deployed_at` ALTER from 0003 — the one production DB already has it."}],"id":"d4","kind":"operational","reason":"the one production DB already has it","revisit":null},{"alternatives":["Store the raw remote URL as-is"],"anchors":[{"end_line":16,"path":"packages/cli/lib/source.js","start_line":9}],"constraints":["Unrecognized URL shapes normalize to null"],"decision":"Normalize git remote URLs (git@, ssh://, https://) into a canonical https://github.com/org/repo form for storage/display","depends_on":[],"evidence":[{"message_id":"m4770","quote":"capture: remote URL (origin, normalized to https://github.com/org/repo), branch, short and full commit SHA, and whether the working tree is dirty"}],"id":"d6","kind":"design","reason":"remote URL (origin, normalized to https://github.com/org/repo)","revisit":null},{"alternatives":["Store only latest provenance on app row without history table"],"anchors":[{"end_line":16,"path":"packages/control-plane/migrations/0003-provenance.sql","start_line":1}],"constraints":[],"decision":"Store one row per deploy in a new deploys table plus mirror the latest provenance fields directly on the app row","depends_on":[],"evidence":[{"message_id":"m4770","quote":"Store repo_url, branch, commit, dirty, deployed_at on a deploys table — one row per deploy, so history is kept — and the latest on the app row."}],"id":"d7","kind":"design","reason":"one row per deploy, so history is kept — and the latest on the app row","revisit":null}],"snapshot":"c0c25e65e9448777880462d03aa6a6a701b18b8a","sources":{"docs/features/source-provenance.md":"1: # Source provenance
2: 
3: Every deploy records where the code came from, so nobody confuses what's deployed with what's on main.
4: 
5: ## CLI
6: 
7: At deploy time, if the directory is inside a git repo, capture: remote URL (origin, normalized to `https://github.com/org/repo`), branch, short and full commit SHA, and whether the working tree is dirty. Send them with the deploy.
8: 
9: Print `✓ source: github.com/acme/tools @ main a3f8e21` and, if dirty, `⚠ uncommitted changes deployed — commit before sharing`. If not a git repo, send nothing and print `source: not a git repo`.
10: 
11: ## Control plane
12: 
13: Store `repo_url`, `branch`, `commit_sha`, `dirty`, `deployed_by`, `deployed_at` on a `deploys` table — one row per deploy, so history is kept — and the latest on the app row. `GET /api/apps/<slug>/deploys` returns the history.
14: 
15: ## Repo visibility
16: 
17: Don't assume. On deploy, the control plane hits `https://api.github.com/repos/<org>/<repo>` unauthenticated; 200 means public, 404 means private or nonexistent, anything else stores unknown. Store `repo_public`. Never store a token.
18: 
19: ## Runbook
20: 
21: A line at the top, under the generated-by line: `> Deployed from github.com/acme/tools @ a3f8e21 (main).` If dirty, the line ends with `Deployed with uncommitted changes.`
22: 
23: ## Deferred (user: "do not do the web UI yet")
24: 
25: - Web UI on `/apps/<slug>`: source line under the title, commit linked to the GitHub tree at the deployed SHA (public repos), `private repo` label otherwise, Deploys tab, runbook Files table linked at the SHA.
26: - Drift: "N commits behind <branch>" from GitHub compare, public repos only, cached hourly.
27: 
28: ## Skipped
29: 
30: - GitLab — GitHub only for visibility and links. <!-- ponytail: normalize handles any host; add GitLab visibility check when a GitLab repo shows up -->
31: - Auto-deploy on push — provenance is recorded, not acted on. <!-- ponytail: needs webhooks + stored tokens; separate feature if ever -->
32: - Private-repo linking via tokens — private repos get plain SHAs, never a stored token. <!-- ponytail: deliberate; tokens in the control plane are a new threat class -->","packages/cli/lib/source.js":"1: 'use strict';
2: const { spawnSync } = require('child_process');
3: 
4: function git(args, cwd) {
5:   const r = spawnSync('git', args, { cwd, encoding: 'utf8', stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'ignore'] });
6:   return r.status === 0 ? r.stdout.trim() : null; // git missing (ENOENT) leaves status null → null
7: }
8: 
9: // git@github.com:org/repo.git | ssh://git@github.com/org/repo.git | https://github.com/org/repo.git
10: // → https://github.com/org/repo. Unrecognized shapes → null.
11: // ponytail: any host normalizes; only github gets visibility checks server-side — GitLab when asked
12: function normalizeRemote(url) {
13:   if (!url) return null;
14:   const m = url.match(/^git@([^:/]+):(.+?)(?:\.git)?\/?$/) || url.match(/^\w+:\/\/(?:[^@/]+@)?([^:/]+)\/(.+?)(?:\.git)?\/?$/);
15:   return m ? `https://${m[1]}/${m[2]}` : null;
16: }
17: 
18: // Where the deploy came from, or null when the directory is not a git repo (or git is absent).
19: function capture(dir) {
20:   if (git(['rev-parse', '--is-inside-work-tree'], dir) !== 'true') return null;
21:   const commit = git(['rev-parse', 'HEAD'], dir);
22:   if (!commit) return null; // repo with no commits yet
23:   return {
24:     repoUrl: normalizeRemote(git(['remote', 'get-url', 'origin'], dir)),
25:     branch: git(['rev-parse', '--abbrev-ref', 'HEAD'], dir), // detached HEAD reads "HEAD"
26:     commit,
27:     shortCommit: git(['rev-parse', '--short', 'HEAD'], dir) || commit.slice(0, 7),
28:     dirty: git(['status', '--porcelain'], dir) !== '',
29:   };
30: }
31: 
32: module.exports = { capture, normalizeRemote };","packages/control-plane/migrations/0003-provenance.sql":"1: -- source provenance: one deploys row per deploy, latest mirrored on the app row (matches schema.sql)
2: CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS deploys (
3:   id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
4:   app_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES apps(id),
5:   repo_url TEXT,
6:   branch TEXT,
7:   commit_sha TEXT,
8:   dirty INTEGER,
9:   deployed_by TEXT NOT NULL,
10:   deployed_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime('now'))
11: );
12: ALTER TABLE apps ADD COLUMN repo_url TEXT;
13: ALTER TABLE apps ADD COLUMN repo_branch TEXT;
14: ALTER TABLE apps ADD COLUMN repo_commit TEXT;
15: ALTER TABLE apps ADD COLUMN repo_dirty INTEGER;
16: ALTER TABLE apps ADD COLUMN repo_public INTEGER;
17: -- no deployed_at ALTER: the production DB already has it (added manually by an early
18: -- runbook experiment, alongside a dead `runbook` column) — schema.sql carries it for fresh DBs","packages/control-plane/src/index.js":"1: // small control plane: CLI API + browser auth wall + router. One Worker + D1.
2: // URLs are path-based (no custom domain): /a/<org>/<app>/... proxies to the app's Fly origin.
3: import { sign, verify, sha256, randomHex } from './token.js';
4: import { ensureFlyApp, ensureVolume, deployTokenFor, startMachine } from './fly.js';
5: import { assumeRole } from './aws.js';
6: import { runReview, generateRunbook } from './review.js';
7: import { parseCron, matches, nextRun } from './cron.js';
